  "body": "### Description\n\nWhen using an OIDC provider as a secondary login method, Synapse will crash if the provider is unavailable at startup.\r\n\r\nThis is rather unfortunate if you are running an IdP alongside Synapse, let's say in a composefile. It required me to build keycloak with a `curl` binary inside the container and implement health checks.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- configure OIDC IdP\r\n- make sure it's unavailable\r\n- start synapse\n\n### Homeserver\n\nN/A\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.81.0\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDocker (matrixdotorg/synapse)\n\n### Database\n\nN/A\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nN/A\n\n### Configuration\n\n```\r\noidc_providers:\r\n  - idp_id: keycloak\r\n    idp_name: \"<snip>\"\r\n    issuer: \"https://<snip/realms/<snip>\"\r\n    client_id: \"synapse\"\r\n    client_secret: \"<snip>\"\r\n    scopes: [\"openid\", \"profile\"]\r\n    user_mapping_provider:\r\n      config:\r\n        localpart_template: \"{{ user.preferred_username }}\"\r\n        display_name_template: \"{{ user.name }}\"\r\n    backchannel_logout_enabled: true\r\n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nN/A\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
